Changes from the original Fish Audio Materials
----------------------------------------------
This fork modifies the inference engine and its interfaces. The main changes
relative to upstream rodrigomatta/s2.cpp are:

- stateful streaming codec decode (stream_begin/stream_decode/stream_end)
  instead of re-decoding the growing prefix for every chunk;
- the first streamed chunk is one frame, so the first PCM byte is emitted
  earlier;
- flash attention and CUDA-graph capture for the decode steps;
- Fast-AR with a KV cache, one codebook-embedding gather per frame, and the
  sampling window kept on the GPU;
- codec decode on a worker thread, overlapped with the AR;
- one-shot reference encoding (`--prepare-voice`) and reuse of the
  reference-prompt KV and of the KV buffer across server requests;
- streaming is the only file path; the offline single-pass path was removed;
- `--seed`, `--stream-file`, `--stream-decode-stride` and the HTTP `params`
  object expose generation parameters that upstream hard-coded;
- concurrent HTTP requests are queued instead of returning 503;
- failures are errors instead of silent fallbacks: a failed GPU codec backend,
  an unreadable reference, a failed prefill or a tokenizer without
  `<|im_end|>` abort with a clear message (CLI exit 1, HTTP 400);
- version string, license headers and runtime DLL deployment added for
  self-contained builds.

